Promote the £19 Home Quote Check Decision Pack payment flow to production.

The implementation uses the existing live Stripe product price price_1UER4fCnmTy7aZ0Hp1zMfDYT and the STRIPE_SECRET_KEY stored as a Cloudflare Worker secret. Checkout is Stripe-hosted, one-off only, and associated to an opaque HQC case reference. Uploaded quote contents are not sent to Stripe.

Payment unlock is not trusted from the return URL: the Cloudflare Worker retrieves the Checkout Session from Stripe server-side and verifies payment status plus matching case/product metadata before the Decision Pack is marked paid. QA/non-production checkout is blocked and existing QA event exclusion remains in place.

Paid Decision Pack actions currently expose second-quote progression, installer clarification questions and a printable Decision Case while retaining evidence guardrails: no design certification, installer approval or grant-eligibility confirmation.

A render-loop defect detected during canary verification was fixed before release by making Decision Pack rendering state-keyed and idempotent.

